  "body": "## What changed\n\n`Top of Model` / `Bottom of Model` resolved through `setup_align::solid_aabb_in`, which walks every `model::model_entities` entry - built-in vises, accessories (soft jaws, plates, chucks) and tagged STEP/mesh fixtures of any setup included. With a vise under the part, a default 2D Contour ran down to the vise base (about 100 mm below the part) and generate reported ok; only verify/post caught it.\n\n- New `setup_align::part_aabb_in(world, setup)`: the bounds of every model that is not a fixture (`FixtureDef`), in the asking setup's frame (the #326 alignment still applies). `solid_aabb_in` now shares its body through a private `models_aabb_in` filter and is unchanged in behaviour.\n- `operation/heights.rs`: `TopOfModel` / `BottomOfModel` and their `missing_source` diagnostic read `part_aabb_in`. These are the only references read from model bounds (stock, work offset and selection read their own sources). The op stamp reads the resolved Z via `resolve_height`, so it follows automatically.\n- Not changed: `model::is_model`, `solid_aabb_in`, the fixture/collision laws. Verify still strikes a pass into the vise.\n- Setup scoping: parts are document-wide (a setup holds the same parts in its own frame) and only fixtures bind to a setup, so leaving every fixture out means a vise in Setup 2 cannot move Setup 1's heights. Recorded in `docs/decisions/1529-heights-exclude-fixtures.md`, along with why the semantics stay \"all parts\" rather than \"the op's source\", and why the #1094 stock-only skip was left out.\n\n## Pins (`crates/app/tests/heights_fixtures.rs`)\n\n| Test | What it pins |\n|---|---|\n| `a_vise_under_the_part_leaves_bottom_of_model_at_the_part_and_the_path_unchanged` | 50 x 50 x 6 block (Z 4..10) plus a 5 in vise with jaw tops at Z 2: refs = (10, 4); the path signature and lowest Z are the same as without the vise |\n| `a_vise_fitted_to_the_stock_leaves_top_of_model_at_the_part_not_the_jaw_tops` | vise `FitStock`, jaws above the part: Top of Model = 10, not the jaw tops |\n| `a_vise_declared_in_setup_two_does_not_move_setup_ones_heights` | vise in Setup2: refs equal the part's in None/Setup1/Setup2; the contour path is the bare one |\n| `a_soft_jaw_a_plate_and_a_tagged_mesh_fixture_are_not_the_model` | soft jaw accessory, 300 x 300 dowel plate, and two imported meshes tagged as fixtures (one under, one over the part): refs = (10, 4) |\n| `the_collision_check_still_sees_the_vise` | a contour taken 3 mm under the part (Z 1, below the jaw tops) still gets `Op: ... strikes a fixture` from `posting::verification_gate` |\n\n**Mutation checks**\n- Revert the filter (`part_aabb_in` keeps every model): all 5 red. Restored: all 5 green.\n- Blind the collision side (`fixture::tagged` returns nothing): only `the_collision_check_still_sees_the_vise` is red, the 4 height pins stay green. Restored: green. So the heights filter and the collision set are pinned independently.\n\n## Gates (macOS arm64, sccache)\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: ok (app lib, fixture_locate_stock, heights_fixtures, heights_selection, setup_align, setup_carry, stock_source_verdict, turning, turning_blade, turning_profile).\n- Extra suites, all green: accessory_collisions, builtin_accessory, builtin_vise, fixture_plate, fixtures, golden_cl, heights, mcp_accessory, mcp_vise, posting, setup_defines_wcs, setup_delete_order, setup_mount_trace, setup_mount, setup_mounts_post, setup_post_options, setup_relative, setup_sheet, setup_stock_source, setup_stock_view, setup_wcs, solid_law_goldens, verify_arc_reading, verify.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Goldens unchanged (they have no fixtures).\n\n## Not exercised\n- UI crate not rebuilt (no UI change; the \"no model loaded\" text is kept verbatim for `ui::operations`' echo test).\n- Not driven over MCP with the issue's exact CLI repro; the pins rebuild that scene through the same commands.\n- Found while fixing this: the GUI's stock \"fit to models\" and the stock info strip still measure the fixtures. Filed as #1538.\n\nBranched from upstream main 41cd9c2.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nChangelog: Top of Model / Bottom of Model heights measure only the part models - a vise, accessory, plate or tagged fixture (in any setup) no longer moves them, so a default cut no longer runs down to the vise base (#1529)\n\nFixes #1529\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n",
